    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Hook execution loop (`async for hook_event in self._hooks_manager.run(...)`) - Hook message injection (`self.messages.append(...)`) - Tool execution (delegates to ToolRuntime) - Event yielding - Middleware execution - Context building - LLM turn dispatch",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Current flow (AgentLoop._conversation_loop)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-13",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "act()  →  _conversation_loop()\n           ├─ create ConversationTurnRuntime\n           ├─ create ConversationRuntime (observer)\n           ├─ cr.set_turn_id()\n           ├─ append user message → yield UserMessageEvent\n           ├─ while not should_break:\n           │    ├─ middleware → cr.decide_after_middleware()\n           │    ├─ first turn: context build\n           │    ├─ _perform_llm_turn()\n           │    ├─ cr.decide_after_model_turn()\n           │    ├─ stop_cancelled? → return\n           │    ├─ stop_completed? → hooks →\n           │    │   cr.decide_after_hook_processing()\n           │    │   retry_hooks? → inject message, continue loop\n           │    ├─ run_tools? → cr.decide_after_tool_batch()\n           │    ├─ cr.decide_after_budget_check()\n           │    └─ fail_budget_exceeded? → return\n           ├─ cr._finish(SUCCESS)\n           └─ turn.mark_outcome(SUCCESS)\n\nact() finally:\n  ├─ self._conversation_runtime = None\n  └─ self._current_turn = None",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "detailed",
        "collapsible": true,
        "collapsed_by_default": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Phase 3 — Loop ownership transfer (planned)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Phase 3 should move the while-loop into `ConversationRuntime.execute_turn()`, but with an important distinction:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **OrchestratorLoop** (renamed from AgentLoop) is the ONLY owner of a full turn loop. Only the desktop cockpit, ACP server, and IDE sidecar should instantiate it.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **SubagentRuntime v1** is built and now owns lifecycle evidence, trace propagation, and explicit tool execution mode markers. `task.py` delegates to `SubagentRuntime`, NOT `AgentLoop`. The `is_subagent=True` pattern is dead and blocked by guard tests.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. **RalphRuntime** should use SubagentRuntime with `profile_kind=AUTONOMOUS_BACKGROUND` — it must never own a full turn loop.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. **Handoff receipts** are required for ownership transfer: owner_before, owner_after, reason, scope, budget, return_condition, trace_id.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "5. AgentLoop → OrchestratorLoop rename should occur AFTER SubagentRuntime exists, to prevent confusion between \"agent\" and \"subagent.\"",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "See `docs/governance/orchestrator-loop-boundary.md` for the full doctrine.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
